    "title": "Kanye West Can No Longer Tour in US",
    "text": "AdvertisementReturn to HomepageTop Stories: Jerome Powell ousting pushPlay Crushable by Candy CrushTrump's new AI Jesus imageU.S.-Iran ceasefireNew Eric Swalwell allegationsThe 'Luddite boyfriend' trendWNBA draft outfitsHeartland severe weather alertsBrian Hooker's messagesMore space eventsU.S. naval blockade A new report alleges Kanye West has been barred from touring in the United States by Live Nation and AEG, underscoring the influence of the dominant concert promoters. Insider Rob Shuter, citing sources on Substack, says Kanye West is banned from touring the U.S., with Live Nation and AEG declining venues, promotion, and infrastructure support. Sources state one cannot tour around them and that both companies have denied permission to perform. West last toured in 2016 on the Saint Pablo Tour supporting The Life of Pablo. A source said this is not his choice amid the forthcoming album Bully, slated for March 20, 2026, noting estimated losses in the tens of millions. Sources added international options are complicated without U.S. backing. The report also says West was banned from this year’s Grammy Awards following a public apology.View comments(22)Terms and Privacy PolicyPrivacy DashboardAbout Our AdsTerms and Privacy PolicyPrivacy DashboardAbout Our AdsRecommended articlesAdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisement",
